## 2. Why Kafka over Redis Streams

| Feature | Redis Streams | Apache Kafka |
|---|---|---|
| Message durability | In-memory (can lose on crash) | Disk-persisted (replayable) |
| Throughput | Good | Excellent (millions/sec) |
| Consumer groups | Basic | Rich (offsets, partitions) |
| Message replay | Limited | ✅ Full replay from any offset |
| Ecosystem | - | ✅ Kafka Connect, Kafka Streams |
| Retention | TTL-based | Configurable (days/forever) |
| Ops complexity | Low | Medium (use Confluent/KRaft mode) |

**Decision:** Use Kafka with **KRaft mode** (no Zookeeper needed since Kafka 3.x).  
Single-broker for dev/MVP → expand to 3 brokers for production.

```
Kafka Topics:
  user.registered          → Notification consumers
  user.role.changed        → Audit + notification
  job.created              → Analytics + AI (compute embeddings)
  job.approved             → Notification (notify employer) + Search index update
  job.scraped              → Admin review queue
  application.created      → Employer notification + Analytics
  application.stage.moved  → Candidate notification + Analytics
  ai.score.request         → AI worker picks up
  ai.score.completed       → Core API updates MongoDB
  notification.email       → Email worker
  notification.push        → FCM push worker
  analytics.event          → Analytics aggregator
```

