## 8. AI Service — Token Optimization & Hybrid Model (Revised)

### 8.1 Hybrid Model Router
```
Task                      Model                  Why
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Resume text parsing       Ollama (Llama 3.1 8B)  Free, fast, private
ATS keyword extraction    Ollama (Llama 3.1 8B)  Free, local inference
ATS scoring computation   Offline (TF-IDF/spaCy) Pure NLP, no LLM
Job matching embeddings   sentence-transformers  Free, local model
AI Chat (basic)           Ollama (Llama 3.1 8B)  Free, adequate quality
AI Chat (premium)         OpenAI GPT-4o          Paid, best quality
Resume summary/advice     OpenAI GPT-4o-mini     Cheaper GPT-4 tier
Interview prep            OpenAI GPT-4o          Best for complex tasks
```

### 8.2 Token Saving Strategies for AI Chat

```
Strategy 1 — Sliding Window Context
  Keep only the last 10 messages in MongoDB recent_messages[]
  Older messages are discarded from active context
  
Strategy 2 — Automatic Context Summarization
  When session exceeds 10 messages:
    → Summarize older messages using Ollama (free!)
    → Store summary in chat_sessions.context_summary
    → Next API call: system prompt = summary + last 10 msgs
    → Old messages removed from active context
  
Strategy 3 — System Prompt Caching (OpenAI feature)
  Long system prompts (resume + JD) are cached by OpenAI
  Repeated calls with same system prompt cost 50% less
  
Strategy 4 — Model Tier Routing
  Simple "what's my ATS score?" → Ollama (free)
  Complex "rewrite my resume for this role" → GPT-4o-mini
  Deep analysis "explain how I compare to industry standards" → GPT-4o

Strategy 5 — Per-User Daily Token Budget
  Track tokens_used per user per day in Redis
  Route to cheaper/offline model when approaching limit
  Show "AI credits" remaining in UI

Result: ~70-80% reduction in paid API token costs
```

### 8.3 AI Chat API Design (SSE Streaming)
```
POST /api/ai/chat
Body: {
  "session_id": "abc123",
  "message": "How can I improve my resume?",
  "context_type": "resume_review" | "career_advice" | "interview_prep"
}

Headers: Accept: text/event-stream  (SSE)

Response stream:
  data: {"token": "Here"}
  data: {"token": " are"}
  data: {"token": " 3 suggestions..."}
  data: {"type": "done", "tokens_used": 312, "model": "gpt-4o-mini"}

Context building (internal):
  1. Fetch chat_sessions by session_id
  2. Build messages array: [system_prompt] + [context_summary?] + recent_messages[-10:]
  3. Route to model based on context_type + user tier
  4. Stream response to client
  5. After stream complete: append to recent_messages[], update context if > 10 msgs
```

