## 9. Scraper Service (Revised — Company Career Pages Only)

### 9.1 Revised Scraping Philosophy
Major platforms (LinkedIn, Indeed, Naukri, Glassdoor) **aggressively block scrapers**:
- IP bans within minutes
- CAPTCHAs, JS challenges (Cloudflare)
- Legal ToS violations
- **Not worth the maintenance cost**

**Revised strategy:**
| Source Type | Method | Scale |
|---|---|---|
| Company career pages | Playwright (configurable templates) | High — add any company |
| Adzuna API | HTTP REST (free 1000 calls/day) | ~50K jobs indexed |
| Jooble API | HTTP REST (free partner access) | Aggregator, global jobs |
| RemoteOK API | HTTP REST (free) | Remote jobs |
| RSS feeds | XML parser (no browser needed) | Many companies offer this |
| Employer direct posting | Your own platform | Most controlled |

### 9.2 Company Career Page Scraper — How It Works

```
Admin adds a company career page:
  URL: "https://careers.infosys.com/jobs"
  Template: "infosys_v1"  (CSS selectors config)

Celery Beat triggers scrape_task every 24 hours
         │
         ▼
Playwright Worker (ISOLATED PROCESS — not in FastAPI)
  ├── Launches Chromium (headless)
  ├── Navigates to careers URL
  ├── Waits for job cards to load (explicit waits, not sleep)
  ├── Extracts: title, location, type, description URL
  ├── For each job: fetch detail page → extract full description
  └── Returns raw job list
         │
         ▼
Normalizer Pipeline
  ├── Clean text (strip HTML, normalize whitespace)
  ├── Dedup: SHA256(title+company+location) → check Redis set
  ├── spaCy NLP: extract skills, experience level from description
  ├── Normalize location → city + country + ISO code
  ├── Normalize salary → detect currency, convert to multi-currency
  └── Status: PENDING_APPROVAL
         │
         ▼
Kafka → job.scraped topic → Admin Service consumer
                              Admin reviews in /admin/job-approvals
                              APPROVE → status: APPROVED → live on platform
                              REJECT → discarded
```

### 9.3 Why Playwright in Separate Process (Not FastAPI)

FastAPI runs on `uvicorn` which has its own `asyncio` event loop.  
Playwright's async API requires **its own event loop context**.  
Running `playwright` directly inside a FastAPI endpoint causes:
- Event loop conflicts → `RuntimeError: This event loop is already running`
- Blocking the API server while browser loads pages
- Memory leaks if browser contexts aren't properly managed

**Solution:** Playwright runs **only inside Celery workers** (separate processes):
```python
# celery_scraper/workers/playwright_worker.py
# This is NOT a FastAPI file — it's a Celery task

from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright  # Sync API in Celery workers

@celery_app.task(name="scrape_company_careers")
def scrape_company_careers(company_config: dict) -> list[dict]:
    with sync_playwright() as p:
        browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)
        page = browser.new_page()
        page.goto(company_config["url"])
        # ... scraping logic
        browser.close()
    return jobs_list

# Scraper API just triggers and monitors:
@router.post("/scraper/trigger")
async def trigger_scrape(company_id: str, admin = Depends(require_role("SUPER_ADMIN"))):
    task = scrape_company_careers.delay(company_config)
    return {"task_id": task.id}
```

