## 10. File Storage — MinIO (Self-Hosted S3)

### Why MinIO
- Runs as a Docker container on your VPS
- S3-compatible API → same boto3/s3fs code works if you later migrate to AWS S3
- Web UI at port 9001 for browsing files
- Object storage: files stored by key, not filesystem path
- Free, open source, production-ready (used by Slack, Verizon, etc.)

### MinIO Buckets
```
recruitzaa-resumes/     → candidate resume PDFs/DOCXs
  {user_id}/{timestamp}_{filename}.pdf
  
recruitzaa-logos/       → company logos, employer profile photos
  companies/{company_id}/logo.png
  
recruitzaa-photos/      → candidate avatar images
  candidates/{user_id}/avatar.jpg
  
recruitzaa-exports/     → generated PDF reports, analytics exports
  exports/{job_id}/applicant_report_{date}.pdf
```

### File Upload Flow
```
Client uploads resume:
  POST /api/profile/resume (multipart/form-data, max 5MB, PDF/DOCX only)
         │
         ▼
  Core API validates: file type, size, MIME sniff
         │
         ▼
  Upload to MinIO: recruitzaa-resumes/{user_id}/{timestamp}_{name}.pdf
         │
         ▼
  Store URL in MongoDB: candidate_profiles.resume_versions[]
         │
         ▼
  Kafka event → ai.parse.request → AI worker parses resume → auto-fill profile
```

