## 16. Concurrency — How We Handle Scale

```
Request comes in → NGINX → FastAPI (Uvicorn async) → async DB call
                                                     (non-blocking)
                                     ↓
                         DB responds → response out

All DB drivers are async:
  PostgreSQL  → asyncpg (connection pool: 20 per worker)
  MongoDB     → Motor   (connection pool: 50 per worker)
  Redis       → aioredis (connection pool: 20 per worker)
  Kafka       → aiokafka (async producer/consumer)

Heavy tasks NEVER run in FastAPI request cycle:
  ATS scoring  → Celery worker (ai_tasks queue)
  Scraping     → Celery worker (scrape_tasks queue)
  Email send   → Celery worker (email_queue)
  Embeddings   → Celery worker (ai_tasks queue)

Gunicorn manages Uvicorn workers per service:
  gunicorn app.main:app \
    --worker-class uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker \
    --workers 4 \          # 2 × CPU cores
    --max-requests 2000    # Recycle worker to prevent memory leaks

Result: Each service handles ~200-400 concurrent connections comfortably.
```

